---
// Hides the viewer's LCARS L-sidebar on routes that mount the React
// viewer (/sessions, /projects, /topics, /practice). Used in concert
// with AppSidebar so the app has a single vertical nav rail (the new
// app-wide left sidebar) instead of two competing rails (AppSidebar
// + the viewer's L-sidebar).
//
// What this hides:
//   * `.lcars-sidebar` (desktop / tablet L-corner sidebar)
//   * `.lcars-sidebar--horizontal` (mobile pill-bar variant)
//
// What this preserves:
//   * `.lcars-top-bar` — search + SCAN LOCAL / UPLOAD ZIP / tier
//     indicator / earthdate. Those are toolbar actions on the viewer
//     itself, not navigation, so they remain useful inside the
//     viewer's main column.
//
// The grid override re-anchors the viewer's top-bar + content column
// to the single-column layout after the sidebar disappears.
---
<style is:global>
  .lcars-sidebar,
  .lcars-sidebar--horizontal {
    display: none !important;
  }

  .lcars-frame {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .lcars-top-bar {
      grid-column: 1 / -1 !important;
    }
    .lcars-content-column {
      grid-column: 1 / -1 !important;
    }
  }
</style>
